  "general_arguments_review": {
    "scalar_loop": "Multiplication of transformed links cancels adjacent inverse frames. P'=g_a P g_a^-1=P for scalar phases; open chains retain different endpoint frames.",
    "matrix_trace": "For finite square matrices, Tr(AB)=sum_i,k A_ik B_ki=Tr(BA); invertible G then gives Tr(GPG^-1)=Tr(P). This is the taught finite identity, not an unavailable source-operator replay.",
    "fixed_trivialization": "If E'=aE and Z'=Z/a for nonzero a, fixed linear tau obeys tau(E')=a tau(E); the scalar product Z'tau(E') remains Ztau(E).",
    "integral_pairing": "n=A3(1,0,0)+A2(0,1,0)+C(1/3,1/4,1/72). Hence <d,n>=A3*d3+A2*d2+C*h is integer under the declared contract. Testing the three generators also shows why one passing n is insufficient.",
    "numerical_scope": "Finite sweeps test all64 quarter-phase frame triples for each of two link lists, and 27 signed integer-coordinate triples for each of four passing dual charges. These checks supplement the displayed algebraic arguments; they are not global source proofs."
  },
